# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings on every platform: the package's launcher (bin/foga.js) and the
# shell scripts must keep their LF (a CRLF shebang line breaks them), and the committed JSON and fixtures hash the same
# everywhere (the bundle hash, the skill package hashes and the fixture's extraction are computed over the bytes).
# A checkout made before this file existed on a Windows machine with core.autocrlf=true should be renormalized:
#   git add --renormalize . && git status
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and the launcher stay executable and LF
*.sh text eol=lf
bin/foga.js text eol=lf

# Binary content, should any be committed (proving material, images)
*.zkey binary
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
